From: yinjiayi <yinjiayi@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: query the inih pkg-config module

The target inih-devel 62 package installs inih.pc, whose Libs directory is
/usr/lib64. Query that module so Findinih receives the supplied include and
library-directory hints. Keep INI support, library-name fallback and the
installed Findinih module; do not bypass the original tests.

The first target configure failed with INIH_LIBRARY missing after a successful
dependency transaction. Its earlier compiler ABI probe also failed; this
compatibility correction does not assert that separate probe's cause or a
successful target outcome. Remove when upstream queries the inih module.

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
--- a/builds/cmake/Modules/Findinih.cmake
+++ b/builds/cmake/Modules/Findinih.cmake
@@ -26,6 +26,6 @@
 find_package(PkgConfig QUIET)
 
-pkg_check_modules(PC_INIH QUIET libinih)
+pkg_check_modules(PC_INIH QUIET inih)
 
 # Look for the header file.
 find_path(INIH_INCLUDE_DIR
